# Motion Blur — a "+" button appends random transaction cards ($ amount, address, emoji) to a 3-card stack; new cards pop in with a keyframe, older ones spring up and blur out (expo-blur intensity via useAnimatedProps) and leave with FadeOutUp.
# What this test covers: the first three adds (no blur yet), the fourth add pushing the first card out (blur 0→50 and
# exiting), steady adds letting each transition finish, a rapid burst of adds that overlaps many exiting
# animations (EXITING_ITEMS_BUFFER=4 window), a very long burst, and a final settle with only three cards left.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/motion-blur"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 800
# First three cards.
press 201 552
wait 700
press 201 552
wait 700
press 201 552
wait 900
# Fourth: the first card blurs out and exits.
press 201 552
wait 1200
# Steady adds.
press 201 552
wait 600
press 201 552
wait 600
press 201 552
wait 1000
# Rapid burst overlapping the exiting animations.
press 201 552 --count 8 --interval-ms 80
wait 1500
# Very long burst.
press 201 552 --count 25 --interval-ms 50
wait 2000
# Single add after the storm.
press 201 552
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
